Package: gbgam
Title: Gradient Boosting for Generalised Additive Models
Version: 1.0.0
Authors@R: 
    person("Antoni", "Sieminski", , "a.m.sieminski@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Fits exponential family generalised additive models by
    component-wise gradient boosting, using penalised regression spline base
    learners built from 'mgcv' smooth terms, including scale-invariant tensor
    product interactions. The effective degrees of freedom of the boosted
    model are tracked during fitting, either exactly or with a randomised
    trace estimator, and are used for adaptive smoothness relaxation of the
    base learners and for AIC-based selection of the stopping iteration. The
    stopping iteration can also be selected by cross-validation or bootstrap
    estimates of the prediction error, and fits can be resumed. An
    approximate covariance matrix of the coefficients can optionally be
    obtained by parametric bootstrap or Bayesian backfitting.
